# Writing Persona & Cover-Letter Constraints

> Copy this file to knowledge/persona.md and tailor it to your voice. The Writer
> reads this verbatim when drafting cover letters.

## Voice & tone
<e.g. warm but professional; confident, not boastful; concise>

## What to emphasize
<e.g. measurable impact, relevant domain experience, motivation for this role>

## What to avoid
- Do not claim any skill or experience not present in cv.md.
- No generic filler ("hard worker", "team player") without evidence.
- <add your own>

## Structure & length
<e.g. 3 short paragraphs, max ~250 words; open with a specific hook tied to the role>

## Hard rules
- Every claim must be grounded in cv.md. If the role requires something not in the
  CV, do not fabricate it; address transferable experience honestly instead.
